Provenance — the rest of the module
-----------------------------------

Unchanged and unaffected by the above.

  - The wire format is clean-room from the format facts documented in
    `minisign.h`/`minisign.c`: the fixed struct layouts
    (`RawPublicKey`/`RawSecretKey`/`RawSignature`), the 2-byte algorithm tags
    ("Ed"/"ED" signing, "Sc"/none KDF, "B2" checksum) and the
    untrusted/trusted comment file framing. A file format has essentially one
    correct expression, so these are uncopyrightable format facts (merger
    doctrine; see CONVENTIONS.md §5) — independently re-derived in Zig and
    cross-checked byte-exact against the real `minisign` 0.12 binary
    (Debian/Ubuntu package) run as a black-box test oracle. The C source WAS
    read directly for the exact byte layout, which root NOTICE §0's
    black-box-oracle carve-out does not cover; that is why it is recorded.
  - Design reference: jedisct1/zig-minisign (ISC License), named as this
    module's Zig-ecosystem sibling for API shape per CONVENTIONS §5. Not read
    line by line; nothing from it is present.
  - scrypt parameter derivation (ops/mem-limit → N/r/p) reuses Zig std's own
    `std.crypto.pwhash.scrypt.Params.fromLimits`, which already matches
    libsodium's `pickparams` algorithm identically. No separate port was
    needed or done.
